Enhancement: Allow choosing columns in `snapshots`

The `--view` option of the `snapshots` command takes a comma separated list of
column names and views. A view is a named collection of columns that is
expanded in place. For example, `--view compact,paths` shows all columns of
the `compact` view plus the paths, and `--view id,time,stored` shows only these
three columns. Available views are `default`, `compact` and `growth`. The
`default` view is unchanged. Available columns are `id`, `time`, `host`,
`tags`, `paths`, `size`, `added`, `stored`, `files`, `duration` and `rate`.
The `rate` is the amount of processed data per second of backup time,
expressed in MiB/s. The
`--compact` option is unchanged and is equivalent to `--view compact`. The
`--json` output is unchanged.

